  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef la_svd_components(matrix: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **SVD Components** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef la_svd_components(matrix: list) -> dict:\n    U, s, Vt = np.linalg.svd(np.array(matrix, dtype=np.float64), full_matrices=False)\n    return {'singular_values': np.round(s, 6).tolist(), 'left_singular_vectors': np.round(U, 6).tolist(), 'right_singular_vectors': np.round(Vt, 6).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
